---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { resolvePath } from '../lib/paths';
---

<BaseLayout title="About">
  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 pt-12 pb-16">
    <h1 data-reveal="1">About</h1>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-8 mt-12 mb-12">
      <div class="md:col-span-2" data-reveal="2">
        <p class="text-base text-space-200 leading-relaxed">
          I'm <strong>Michael Kuhl</strong>, a graduate student in the MIT Department
          of Aeronautics and Astronautics, working in the <strong>Space
          Telecommunications, Astronomy and Radiation Laboratory (STAR Lab)</strong>
          under <strong>Prof. Kerri Cahoy</strong>.
        </p>

        <p class="text-base text-space-200 leading-relaxed mt-4">
          My research centers on in-space assembly and deployment of modular spacecraft.
          I'm the lead student on <strong>ORLO (Orbital Locker)</strong>, a free-flying
          robotic system for autonomous assembly of CubeSats and large tiled structures
          in orbit. With labmates Jonah Goldstein and Prof. Cahoy, I published
          <strong>"Design and Validation of a Modular CubeSat Framework for In-Space
          Assembly"</strong> at SmallSat 2026, describing four standardized module types
          and qualification testing to Falcon-9 secondary-payload structural standards
          (fundamental frequencies &gt; 45 Hz, frequency shift &lt; 2.5%). ORLO has
          already demonstrated a full 72-second autonomous assembly during a
          zero-gravity parabolic flight.
        </p>

        <p class="text-base text-space-200 leading-relaxed mt-4">
          Before coming to MIT, I built a satellite capable of assembling other
          satellites as my senior thesis at Harvard SEAS — foundational hardware and
          systems thinking that led directly to the ORLO project.
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-8 mb-4">This class</h2>
        <p class="text-base text-space-200 leading-relaxed">
          MIT 16.S893 applies AI agents to real research problems. For me, that's ORLO:
          it works in the lab, but its perception and planning are brittle in ways that
          matter for real missions. This project uses the agent patterns from the course
          to close that gap — building the perceive-detect-replan loop that turns a
          brittle offline pipeline into something that notices failures and responds to them
          in real time.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-4">
        <div class="border border-orbit/20 overflow-hidden" data-reveal="3">
          <img
            src={resolvePath('/images/Grad.jpeg')}
            alt="Michael Kuhl, MIT"
            class="w-full h-auto"
          />
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-space-400 italic">MIT, 2026</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 data-reveal="4">Beyond research</h2>
    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-4 gap-4 mb-8" data-reveal="4">
      <div class="border border-orbit/15 p-3">
        <img
          src={resolvePath('/images/Hockey.jpeg')}
          alt="Hockey"
          class="w-full h-auto mb-2"
        />
        <p class="text-xs text-space-400 m-0">Club hockey</p>
      </div>
      <div class="border border-orbit/15 p-3">
        <img
          src={resolvePath('/images/Surf.jpeg')}
          alt="Surfing"
          class="w-full h-auto mb-2"
        />
        <p class="text-xs text-space-400 m-0">Surfing</p>
      </div>
      <div class="border border-orbit/15 p-3">
        <img
          src={resolvePath('/images/Fish.jpeg')}
          alt="Fishing"
          class="w-full h-auto mb-2"
        />
        <p class="text-xs text-space-400 m-0">Fishing</p>
      </div>
      <div class="border border-orbit/15 p-3">
        <img
          src={resolvePath('/images/Travel.jpeg')}
          alt="Travel"
          class="w-full h-auto mb-2"
        />
        <p class="text-xs text-space-400 m-0">Travel</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 data-reveal="5">Contact & links</h2>
    <div class="space-y-2 text-base text-space-300" data-reveal="5">
      <p>
        <strong>GitHub:</strong>{' '}
        <a href="https://github.com/michaelkuhl10">@michaelkuhl10</a>
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>MIT STAR Lab:</strong>{' '}
        <a href="https://starlab.mit.edu">starlab.mit.edu</a>
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Publications:</strong>{' '}
        <a href="https://dspace.mit.edu">MIT DSpace</a> (ORLO papers and thesis)
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
